  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Bae Systems Information and Electronic Systems Integration has $799M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company received 171 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $4.7M. Obligations are down 8.9% year over year. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Historical annual obligations show a peak in FY24 at $1.1B and a sequence of prior years recorded as $700M in FY21, $689M in FY22, $644M in FY23, and $878M in FY25. The FY2026 to date obligations concentrate in a few NAICS markets: Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $344M, Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $165M, and Other Electronic Component Manufacturing at $147M. Aircraft Manufacturing and Engineering Services recorded $55.6M and $54.5M respectively. The dataset notes award-value figures in some tables are total contract values and that current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How did obligations change compared with prior years?",
        "body": "Bae Systems Information and Electronic Systems Integration obligated $799M in FY2026 to date, down 8.9% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations were $700M in FY21, $689M in FY22, $644M in FY23, $1.1B in FY24, and $878M in FY25. The FY24 total of $1.1B is the largest annual figure in the listed series."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets drive FY2026 to date obligations?",
        "body": "Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing leads with $344M in obligations. Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing and Other Electronic Component Manufacturing follow with $165M and $147M respectively. Aircraft Manufacturing and Engineering Services account for $55.6M and $54.5M of obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
